======================================================================
                  Install instructions for Tclpp
======================================================================

	1. Requirements
	2. Configuration
	   2.1 Unix
	   2.2 Windows

1. Requirements

    Tclpp requires Tcl version 8.0 or later. Upon configuration, the
    existence of tclsh with the correct version will be checked. No
    other requirement exist.
    Upon compilation, it is requried to have the source distribution
    of Tcl/Tk installed.

2. Configuration

    2.1 Unix

        From within the "unix" directory, call

	    ./configure

        This will configure the sources according to the system configuration
        and checks if this system is able to use Tclpp. The following options
        are useful for fine tuning the configuration:

	    --enable-gcc		force to use the GNU-C compiler
	    --enable-symbols	build with debugging symbols
	    --enable-shared		build libtclpp as a shared library
	    --with-tcl=DIR		use Tcl 8.0 libraries from DIR

        After successful configuration, call

	    make

        to create the Tclpp package index file, documentation and to run all
        the verification tests.

        The Tcl-shell will be available in the 'src' directory
    
        To install the software, call

	    make install

    2.2 Windows

	From within the "win" directory, perform

	    copy makefile.vc makefile
	
	and edit this makefile. Only the first part of this makefile need
	to be changed to match your development environment. The makefile
	and the sources have been tested with Microsoft Visual C++ version 6.
	After that, call

	    nmake

	to build the DLL's and the executables. If you wish to make the
	help files, you should invoke

	    nmake winhelp

